Subject: [PATCH 36/37] s13d g4 cont4: the leftward row through the mirror
 lockstep; exists_zoneRebalanceTM proved

The leftward row is the rightward row's machine with tape 0's moves reversed, run on the data
with every track's sides exchanged: the mirror is one step per step (Turing.Contract.lockstep),
the mirrored zoned tape is the exchanged data's (zr_mirror_tape), and Turing.zoneRebalance_false
identifies the endpoint. Both rows meet the target's fields at the constant 2300, and the row's
states are finite with decidable equality.

